{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBeam","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that the beam number does not distinguish sets of beams that overlap, as it does for slur and other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements. Beaming groups are distinguished by being in different voices and\/or the presence or absence of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grace and cue elements."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beams that have a begin value can also have a fan attribute to indicate accelerandos and ritardandos using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fanned beams. The fan attribute may also be used with a continue value if the fanning direction changes on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that note. The value is “none” if not specified."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The repeater attribute has been deprecated in MusicXML 3.0. Formerly used for tremolos, it needs to be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified with a “yes” value for each beam using it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"code":"<beam>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbeam"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Beam values include begin, continue, end, forward hook, and backward hook. Up to eight concurrent beams are","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text"